1
00:00:01,721 --> 00:00:03,889
[opening theme music playing]

2
00:01:31,018 --> 00:01:35,940
UPON A NEST OF DRIED NOODLES

3
00:01:36,023 --> 00:01:38,025
DRAMA CLUB

4
00:01:38,108 --> 00:01:39,109
[Fudge] We're off.

5
00:01:39,193 --> 00:01:41,195
[Aoba] Bill, lock up when you're done.

6
00:01:41,278 --> 00:01:42,196
FESTIVAL OF THE METEOR

7
00:01:42,279 --> 00:01:44,448
[Bill] Sure thing! Just finishing up.

8
00:01:45,574 --> 00:01:46,700
[sighs]

9
00:01:46,784 --> 00:01:51,205
But before I do,
time for a little bite to eat.

10
00:01:51,288 --> 00:01:53,124
[Bill humming]

11
00:01:55,042 --> 00:01:56,544
{\an8}ORIGINAL EGG-FLAVOR ABURA SOBA

12
00:01:56,627 --> 00:01:57,920
[screams]

13
00:01:59,046 --> 00:02:00,798
[tense breathing]

14
00:02:00,881 --> 00:02:01,799
[Bill] <i>No way...</i>

15
00:02:02,550 --> 00:02:04,969
<i>Uh... It's gotta be dead.</i>

16
00:02:05,052 --> 00:02:05,970
[gasps]

17
00:02:07,888 --> 00:02:11,142
<i>So if I ate this... would that be bad?</i>

18
00:02:12,017 --> 00:02:14,937
<i>Bill the Bengal Tiger,
you better think about this.</i>

19
00:02:15,855 --> 00:02:17,648
<i>Devouring is a serious crime,</i>

20
00:02:17,731 --> 00:02:23,404
<i>so that's why carnivores stick to getting
our protein from milk and eggs instead.</i>

21
00:02:23,487 --> 00:02:26,448
<i>This is a tricky one.</i>

22
00:02:26,532 --> 00:02:29,118
<i>Can I eat it? Or not?</i>

23
00:02:29,827 --> 00:02:34,498
<i>Well, I mean, look.
This tiny thing's probably going to die.</i>

24
00:02:34,582 --> 00:02:36,208
<i>I have to say...</i>

25
00:02:36,292 --> 00:02:37,293
[salivating]

26
00:02:37,376 --> 00:02:39,879
<i>It would probably be crazy delicious.</i>

27
00:02:40,880 --> 00:02:43,924
[Louis] Honestly, I couldn't care less
about you swallowing some animal blood

28
00:02:44,008 --> 00:02:45,467
to pep yourself up.

29
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:50,139
{\an8}[Bill] <i>Apologies, buddy.
This is just who I am, Louis.</i>

30
00:02:50,222 --> 00:02:52,892
<i>I'm a fan of instant gratification.</i>

31
00:02:52,975 --> 00:02:56,854
<i>And if I'm being real with myself,
I half-ass everything.</i>

32
00:02:56,937 --> 00:03:00,649
<i>I guess I'm just carnivore trash
who loves eating meat!</i>

33
00:03:00,733 --> 00:03:02,985
- [Pina] Are you going to eat that?
- [Bill exclaims]

34
00:03:03,068 --> 00:03:06,447
- Wow, first time I've seen this.
- [grunts in frustration]

35
00:03:06,530 --> 00:03:09,533
I've heard of situations like this
occasionally, but...

36
00:03:09,617 --> 00:03:11,869
[stuttering] I thought you went home!

37
00:03:11,952 --> 00:03:13,996
Ah, now I see.

38
00:03:14,079 --> 00:03:15,998
You were hoping nobody would be around

39
00:03:16,081 --> 00:03:17,917
{\an8}to see you end that thing's life,
am I right?

40
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:18,876
{\an8}[Bill seethes]

41
00:03:18,959 --> 00:03:22,046
{\an8}I'll be able to use this
when I play a carnivore.

42
00:03:22,129 --> 00:03:23,005
{\an8}[Bill grunting]

43
00:03:23,088 --> 00:03:24,381
{\an8}Go ahead, don't let me stop you.

44
00:03:24,465 --> 00:03:26,592
{\an8}- As if I'm not even here.
- Huh?

45
00:03:26,675 --> 00:03:28,135
{\an8}I'll be taking a few notes.

46
00:03:28,218 --> 00:03:29,053
{\an8}[Bill growls]

47
00:03:29,136 --> 00:03:33,057
{\an8}The world is strange...
It's unfair and cruel.

48
00:03:33,140 --> 00:03:34,058
[Bill] Huh?

49
00:03:34,141 --> 00:03:38,604
[Pina] Riz, for example, is sitting
in juvie right now for eating a classmate.

50
00:03:38,687 --> 00:03:40,814
Meanwhile, you'll eat that thing,

51
00:03:40,898 --> 00:03:45,402
and your peaceful life at school
continues on as if it never happened.

52
00:03:45,486 --> 00:03:47,154
Of course I won't eat it!

53
00:03:47,238 --> 00:03:50,658
Oh. If that's the case,
what are you going to do?

54
00:03:50,741 --> 00:03:52,826
Save the thing, obviously!

55
00:03:52,910 --> 00:03:57,790
Wow! Carnivores are amazingly complex.
I'm learning a lot.

56
00:03:57,873 --> 00:03:58,707
[Bill growls]

57
00:03:58,791 --> 00:04:02,169
I didn't realize you had
as many layers as you do stripes.

58
00:04:02,253 --> 00:04:04,004
- You little...
- [chick squeaks]

59
00:04:04,088 --> 00:04:04,922
- Hmm?
- Huh?

60
00:04:05,005 --> 00:04:06,257
[squeaking weakly]

61
00:04:06,340 --> 00:04:07,549
[Pina] Oh, boy.

62
00:04:09,134 --> 00:04:10,803
[gentle music playing]

63
00:04:12,513 --> 00:04:13,931
Ah...

64
00:04:14,014 --> 00:04:15,182
[chuckles]

65
00:04:15,266 --> 00:04:18,143
[Bill] You're all warm and cozy now,
I bet.

66
00:04:19,019 --> 00:04:21,772
It says the parent bird's body heat is...

67
00:04:21,855 --> 00:04:22,898
[chick squeaking]

68
00:04:23,524 --> 00:04:24,358
It's burning!

69
00:04:24,441 --> 00:04:25,859
[exclaims]

70
00:04:25,943 --> 00:04:27,319
{\an8}[grunting]

71
00:04:27,903 --> 00:04:29,113
[squeaks]

72
00:04:30,739 --> 00:04:32,449
Sure you weren't making yakitori?

73
00:04:32,533 --> 00:04:34,076
Not funny, Pina.

74
00:04:34,159 --> 00:04:36,620
But, speaking of yakitori,
what's this thing eat?

75
00:04:36,704 --> 00:04:38,080
Let's see.

76
00:04:38,163 --> 00:04:40,958
What does a baby chick eat?

77
00:04:42,334 --> 00:04:44,003
A FEW DAYS LATER

78
00:04:44,086 --> 00:04:48,132
[Kai] I mean, come on,
I just wish those two would cut it out.

79
00:04:48,215 --> 00:04:50,217
[Fudge] Huh? Juno and Pina?

80
00:04:50,301 --> 00:04:54,722
Yeah. The tension between them is totally
ruining the vibe, if you ask me.

81
00:04:54,805 --> 00:04:57,766
Well, hopefully
those two will get all that sorted out.

82
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:00,019
If they don't, we're screwed.

83
00:05:00,728 --> 00:05:01,812
[exclaims]

84
00:05:03,897 --> 00:05:05,899
Sorry about that. My bad, you guys.

85
00:05:05,983 --> 00:05:09,236
Hey! You know how much it would've cost
if you broke one of our lights?

86
00:05:09,320 --> 00:05:11,196
Like it would've mattered.

87
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:13,824
You know the principal
would just buy you babies a new one.

88
00:05:13,907 --> 00:05:15,326
What?

89
00:05:15,409 --> 00:05:19,204
Everyone at school knows you rejects
are all the principal's little pets.

90
00:05:19,288 --> 00:05:22,624
[laughs] Even after that devouring,
you little brats are still spoiled.

91
00:05:22,708 --> 00:05:25,085
All you carnivores and herbivores
playing pretend.

92
00:05:25,169 --> 00:05:28,088
So who's gonna be on the menu
at your next rehearsal?

93
00:05:28,172 --> 00:05:29,340
[Kai] All right, enough!

94
00:05:29,423 --> 00:05:30,924
Your paws are gonna look good

95
00:05:31,008 --> 00:05:32,176
- shoved up your--
- [Bill] Cut it out!

96
00:05:32,259 --> 00:05:33,552
Huh?

97
00:05:36,472 --> 00:05:39,975
The drama club president's
here to save the day.

98
00:05:42,019 --> 00:05:43,437
Have you guys had lunch yet?

99
00:05:45,981 --> 00:05:47,232
[all exclaim]

100
00:05:47,316 --> 00:05:48,442
Those look sharp.

101
00:05:48,525 --> 00:05:49,443
Yeah. Time to go.

102
00:05:49,526 --> 00:05:52,696
[basketball player laughing]
Don't know about you, but I like living.

103
00:05:53,363 --> 00:05:57,076
We gotta keep our heads down.
Let's just focus on the show.

104
00:05:57,159 --> 00:05:58,577
Yeah, but come on...

105
00:05:58,660 --> 00:06:01,497
[Bill] Hurry up,
this stuff needs to get to the club room.

106
00:06:01,580 --> 00:06:05,417
Hey, you're stronger than all of us.
Wanna lend a hand?

107
00:06:06,126 --> 00:06:07,878
[Bill] I'm busy right now.

108
00:06:10,214 --> 00:06:12,007
[Kai] I wonder what's going on with him.

109
00:06:12,091 --> 00:06:15,719
I heard he spaced out in class,
and the professor called him on it.

110
00:06:15,803 --> 00:06:17,387
And he hasn't been at his dorm much.

111
00:06:17,471 --> 00:06:19,598
I bet it's got something
to do with a girl.

112
00:06:19,681 --> 00:06:20,933
So who we talkin' about?

113
00:06:21,016 --> 00:06:22,184
[Aoba, Fudge and Kai exclaim]

114
00:06:22,267 --> 00:06:25,813
It felt like I saw the start
of an argument from over there. [chuckles]

115
00:06:25,896 --> 00:06:27,648
I came over hoping to be entertained.

116
00:06:27,731 --> 00:06:29,399
[Kai] It wasn't a show for you!

117
00:06:29,483 --> 00:06:30,692
Oh, really?

118
00:06:31,610 --> 00:06:33,987
Bill doesn't seem like himself lately.

119
00:06:34,655 --> 00:06:37,574
[Fudge] He doesn't really strike me
as the broody type.

120
00:06:37,658 --> 00:06:39,034
[Pina] Hmm.

121
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:42,830
- [Bill grunting]
- [scraping]

122
00:06:45,999 --> 00:06:47,543
Hmm?

123
00:06:48,293 --> 00:06:49,419
[frustrated sigh]

124
00:06:50,546 --> 00:06:53,423
[Bill] <i>Ugh, why is this so tough?</i>

125
00:06:54,800 --> 00:06:57,636
[chirping]

126
00:06:59,847 --> 00:07:02,933
Sorry, I couldn't find very much today.

127
00:07:03,016 --> 00:07:05,519
Don't choke on this, huh? Open up.

128
00:07:06,353 --> 00:07:07,271
[gulps]

129
00:07:07,354 --> 00:07:10,274
[chirping]

130
00:07:10,357 --> 00:07:12,776
{\an8}Yeah, I knew it wouldn't be enough.

131
00:07:12,860 --> 00:07:14,653
{\an8}[Pina] Apparently
they like eating rice too.

132
00:07:14,736 --> 00:07:16,321
[exclaims] You scared me!

133
00:07:16,405 --> 00:07:17,322
[Pina] Hello.

134
00:07:17,406 --> 00:07:19,533
Aoba's the one that told me
they like rice.

135
00:07:19,616 --> 00:07:21,368
[Bill grunts] You told Aoba?

136
00:07:21,452 --> 00:07:24,455
I didn't tell him about your little guy.

137
00:07:24,538 --> 00:07:26,498
I told him I only wanted to know

138
00:07:26,582 --> 00:07:29,418
just in case the day came
when I happen to get a bird pregnant.

139
00:07:29,501 --> 00:07:31,420
[sighs in relief] Thanks for that.

140
00:07:36,633 --> 00:07:38,760
Would you look at that. Isn't it great?

141
00:07:38,844 --> 00:07:40,512
Huh? What's great?

142
00:07:40,596 --> 00:07:42,014
That it's looking healthy.

143
00:07:42,890 --> 00:07:44,016
You are happy, right?

144
00:07:44,099 --> 00:07:47,728
Of course I'm happy! However...

145
00:07:47,811 --> 00:07:48,979
However?

146
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:53,400
- No, it's nothing.
- Hmm.

147
00:07:54,151 --> 00:07:55,152
[Bill] You can go.

148
00:07:55,235 --> 00:07:56,945
[Pina] I'm not here for this little bird,

149
00:07:57,029 --> 00:07:59,740
I told you I'm observing you
for my acting research.

150
00:08:00,699 --> 00:08:03,327
[Bill] It's weird seeing
your tender side come out.

151
00:08:03,410 --> 00:08:05,496
[Pina] What? I'm just calm.

152
00:08:05,579 --> 00:08:11,293
Sometimes I'm even able to scare myself,
but this bird has no idea what fear is.

153
00:08:11,376 --> 00:08:12,628
[chick squeaks]

154
00:08:12,711 --> 00:08:15,088
[Bill] Do you know how close I came
to eating you?

155
00:08:15,172 --> 00:08:16,006
[chirps]

156
00:08:16,590 --> 00:08:18,300
[Bill chuckles softly]

157
00:08:25,057 --> 00:08:26,892
[Deshico] Ah, let's see...

158
00:08:27,893 --> 00:08:28,977
Mm-hmm.

159
00:08:29,645 --> 00:08:30,812
Mm.

160
00:08:31,730 --> 00:08:32,981
Mmm-hmm...

161
00:08:34,733 --> 00:08:35,609
Ugh.

162
00:08:35,692 --> 00:08:36,818
[spitting]

163
00:08:36,902 --> 00:08:38,904
The east side is certainly no good.

164
00:08:39,530 --> 00:08:41,031
Well, this is an off-year, remember.

165
00:08:41,114 --> 00:08:44,493
But that doesn't mean
quality can have an off-year, too.

166
00:08:44,576 --> 00:08:45,744
[inhales]

167
00:08:45,827 --> 00:08:49,873
By the way, did the Shishi-Gumi
come to pay for the Melda?

168
00:08:49,957 --> 00:08:53,210
No. They were busy
with the Masquerade Party,

169
00:08:53,293 --> 00:08:54,836
then said they were short on cash.

170
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:59,132
And here I was thinking that
the lions would make a good target.

171
00:08:59,216 --> 00:09:01,969
The problem is their leader, isn't it?

172
00:09:02,052 --> 00:09:05,556
And speaking of,
I heard their boss is missing.

173
00:09:05,639 --> 00:09:06,974
[chuckles]

174
00:09:07,057 --> 00:09:11,520
There's a reason I've been doing so much
research into hybrids like him, you know.

175
00:09:11,603 --> 00:09:16,858
We'll just have to make sure
that Melon takes responsibility.

176
00:09:19,152 --> 00:09:23,824
[Corne] The first victim was a herbivore.
The culprit, a carnivore.

177
00:09:23,907 --> 00:09:24,783
SUSPECT DEAD, VICTIM DEAD

178
00:09:24,866 --> 00:09:26,577
[Corne] Then it was lights out
for that same carnivore.

179
00:09:28,370 --> 00:09:30,998
Which brings us to this delightful case.

180
00:09:31,582 --> 00:09:34,209
We're seeing the same pattern
pop up again.

181
00:09:34,293 --> 00:09:36,628
The carnivore culprit
turns into the victim.

182
00:09:36,712 --> 00:09:40,591
Are we seeing a vigilante
punishing devourers then?

183
00:09:40,674 --> 00:09:41,842
[Corne sighs]

184
00:09:41,925 --> 00:09:46,305
Maybe we have a psychic vigilante
who knew they'd be committing a devouring.

185
00:09:46,388 --> 00:09:47,347
[mouse clicks]

186
00:09:48,181 --> 00:09:50,684
[Corne] And in this morning's case,
our greatest hits again.

187
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:51,852
[mouse clicks]

188
00:09:52,811 --> 00:09:55,314
- [mouse clicks]
- [Corne] Look what we have here.

189
00:09:55,397 --> 00:09:56,690
[Yahya] Kines?

190
00:09:58,150 --> 00:10:00,902
Their entire stock
was supposed to be discontinued.

191
00:10:02,070 --> 00:10:04,656
So where are they getting their supply?

192
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:06,742
I've got a theory on the victims--

193
00:10:06,825 --> 00:10:08,368
- [yelps]
- [thud]

194
00:10:08,994 --> 00:10:10,787
[Corne groaning] I'm gonna feel that one.

195
00:10:10,871 --> 00:10:15,083
Reason 100 I hate using a mouse.
Oh, that smarts.

196
00:10:16,877 --> 00:10:19,212
[panting]

197
00:10:20,922 --> 00:10:21,923
Ms. Seven!

198
00:10:22,007 --> 00:10:23,091
[Seven] Huh?

199
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:27,471
[sighs in relief]
Legoshi, you came all the way to see me?

200
00:10:27,554 --> 00:10:32,601
I took it upon myself to call him.
They say the more the merrier, right?

201
00:10:33,352 --> 00:10:37,272
- Are you okay? I...
- Ah, I just discovered it.

202
00:10:37,356 --> 00:10:39,066
That's all that happened.

203
00:10:39,149 --> 00:10:42,986
This morning, when I stopped by the shop,
it was such an awful scene.

204
00:10:43,070 --> 00:10:45,906
And so I ended up fainting
right on the spot.

205
00:10:45,989 --> 00:10:49,201
Oh... Ms. Seven, are you hurt?

206
00:10:49,284 --> 00:10:51,578
Ah, I'm fine. Not hurt at all.

207
00:10:51,662 --> 00:10:52,663
[Legoshi sighs in relief]

208
00:10:52,746 --> 00:10:54,289
That's great!

209
00:10:57,501 --> 00:10:59,461
I hear the crime scene's weird.

210
00:10:59,544 --> 00:11:03,632
The culprit devoured the shop clerk
and then was killed by someone else.

211
00:11:03,715 --> 00:11:07,302
And whoever did it,
they still haven't found him or her.

212
00:11:07,386 --> 00:11:10,972
[Legoshi] Wait, so, you're saying
there were two separate murders?

213
00:11:11,056 --> 00:11:14,893
It seems the shop clerk
was devoured by her own lover.

214
00:11:14,976 --> 00:11:17,312
An interspecies couple, yeah.

215
00:11:17,396 --> 00:11:18,772
Oh...

216
00:11:18,855 --> 00:11:22,859
[Seven] There's been a lot of devourings
lately between interspecies couples.

217
00:11:22,943 --> 00:11:24,236
[Legoshi groans uneasily]

218
00:11:24,319 --> 00:11:25,695
[Seven] It makes you wonder

219
00:11:25,779 --> 00:11:28,907
if interspecies relationships
can ever be safe.

220
00:11:28,990 --> 00:11:31,118
Or are they always deadly?

221
00:11:31,201 --> 00:11:33,954
Well, I guess that's for them
to figure out themselves.

222
00:11:34,037 --> 00:11:35,956
[sighs softly]
Yeah, you're right about that.

223
00:11:36,039 --> 00:11:39,709
But anyway there's nothing to worry about.
I'm totally fine. Really.

224
00:11:40,335 --> 00:11:41,211
Right.

225
00:11:41,294 --> 00:11:44,965
I'm glad to hear that.
If you need some quiet time, I understand.

226
00:11:45,048 --> 00:11:46,299
Yeah.

227
00:11:46,383 --> 00:11:49,678
You show concern in a different way
than most carnivores do.

228
00:11:49,761 --> 00:11:51,596
[Legoshi] Oh, uh...

229
00:11:51,680 --> 00:11:53,098
It was sweet of you to check on me.

230
00:11:53,181 --> 00:11:55,225
[Legoshi] Oh, uh...

231
00:11:55,308 --> 00:11:57,394
[Legoshi exclaims]

232
00:11:57,477 --> 00:11:59,312
I've gotta make my way back to work.

233
00:11:59,396 --> 00:12:02,232
I'm glad you're okay.
Call me if you need anything.

234
00:12:02,315 --> 00:12:03,733
Bye!

235
00:12:03,817 --> 00:12:05,610
[rushed footsteps]

236
00:12:05,694 --> 00:12:08,947
Legoshi. Feelings make him bashful.

237
00:12:09,030 --> 00:12:10,115
Ah.

238
00:12:13,160 --> 00:12:14,995
{\an8}[Lisa] Sorry for dragging you along.

239
00:12:15,078 --> 00:12:16,705
Is this guy really that cool?

240
00:12:16,788 --> 00:12:18,123
He's amazing.

241
00:12:18,206 --> 00:12:21,209
I saw him on the news and I was like,
"Oh, there's my boy!"

242
00:12:21,293 --> 00:12:23,628
So cool, and it doesn't hurt
that he's such a cutie.

243
00:12:23,712 --> 00:12:25,338
- [Haru laughs]
- Ah, over there!

244
00:12:25,422 --> 00:12:29,050
- [music playing]
- So, uh, what sport does he play?

245
00:12:29,759 --> 00:12:32,429
[Lisa] Well, I don't think
he's really a sports guy...

246
00:12:33,221 --> 00:12:34,931
Look! There he is!

247
00:12:35,015 --> 00:12:36,433
What?

248
00:12:38,727 --> 00:12:39,936
[host] All right, everyone!

249
00:12:40,020 --> 00:12:43,190
Today's guest is our ambassador
for the Zoolympic bid,

250
00:12:43,273 --> 00:12:45,650
and I can't think
of a better choice to represent us!

251
00:12:45,734 --> 00:12:49,905
He's the heir of The Horns Conglomerate.
It's Louis the red deer!

252
00:12:49,988 --> 00:12:51,406
It's a pleasure to be here.

253
00:12:51,490 --> 00:12:52,324
I LOVE LOUIS

254
00:12:52,407 --> 00:12:53,867
[host] We're all thrilled to be empowered

255
00:12:53,950 --> 00:12:56,578
by the wisdom
I'm sure we'll receive from our guest.

256
00:12:56,661 --> 00:12:57,871
Ready, and...

257
00:12:57,954 --> 00:12:59,998
- Empower!
- [recording] <i>Empower!</i>

258
00:13:00,665 --> 00:13:05,212
[Haru] <i>I had no idea he'd been so...
public lately.</i>

259
00:13:05,295 --> 00:13:07,172
<i>He's really in another galaxy now.</i>

260
00:13:07,255 --> 00:13:08,632
<i>- I mean, he always was.</i>
- [host] All right,

261
00:13:08,715 --> 00:13:11,510
we've got some great questions
from our listeners! Question one.

262
00:13:11,593 --> 00:13:15,388
Were you only chosen as ambassador
because you're related to a big sponsor?

263
00:13:15,472 --> 00:13:16,640
[Louis] Not at all.

264
00:13:16,723 --> 00:13:20,268
Just as we can't choose what species
we are before we're born,

265
00:13:20,352 --> 00:13:22,521
we also can't choose our family, right?

266
00:13:23,230 --> 00:13:26,483
It just so happens
that my father is chairman of Horns.

267
00:13:26,566 --> 00:13:28,568
[recording] <i>Empower!</i>

268
00:13:28,652 --> 00:13:31,613
Have you ever seen more amazing eyelashes?

269
00:13:31,696 --> 00:13:33,114
I guess...

270
00:13:33,198 --> 00:13:36,326
And I heard you had
your own fan club in high school?

271
00:13:36,409 --> 00:13:37,911
Where'd you hear something like that?

272
00:13:37,994 --> 00:13:42,290
I'm sure you were around all walks of life
in school, like carnivore ladies, right?

273
00:13:42,374 --> 00:13:45,794
Well, some carnivore gals
made their way here to see you!

274
00:13:45,877 --> 00:13:49,673
Someone's species
is really nothing more than an attribute.

275
00:13:49,756 --> 00:13:53,176
In my opinion, the path
we choose to walk is what matters.

276
00:13:53,260 --> 00:13:55,679
The choices we make as individuals,

277
00:13:55,762 --> 00:13:57,889
not what species you happen to be.

278
00:13:57,973 --> 00:14:00,100
[recording] <i>Empower!</i>

279
00:14:00,183 --> 00:14:01,434
So great!

280
00:14:01,518 --> 00:14:04,688
Now let's dig a little bit deeper.
[chuckles]

281
00:14:04,771 --> 00:14:07,607
I'm gonna read an email we got. Uh...

282
00:14:07,691 --> 00:14:11,403
"I'm afraid to tell my friends and family
I fell in love with a carnivore."

283
00:14:11,486 --> 00:14:13,446
How would you handle this, Louis?

284
00:14:16,700 --> 00:14:18,451
[soft music playing]

285
00:14:18,535 --> 00:14:19,870
{\an8}Well, I have a friend...

286
00:14:19,953 --> 00:14:20,996
Huh?

287
00:14:21,079 --> 00:14:23,665
- Their worry has been weighing on them.
- Hmm.

288
00:14:23,748 --> 00:14:26,167
They're scared that
living the way they want

289
00:14:26,251 --> 00:14:29,254
might cause trouble
for their parents or those close to them.

290
00:14:29,337 --> 00:14:30,463
[host] Oh...

291
00:14:31,131 --> 00:14:34,676
{\an8}And they weren't sure if the thing
they actually wanted was worth

292
00:14:34,759 --> 00:14:37,053
{\an8}- all the trouble that would come--
- [recording] <i>Empower!</i>

293
00:14:37,137 --> 00:14:38,430
Oh, I didn't mean to press that!

294
00:14:38,513 --> 00:14:41,391
[chuckles] I don't think we missed
any wisdom from me.

295
00:14:41,474 --> 00:14:44,728
[host] Okay! Let's move on to a request.

296
00:14:47,939 --> 00:14:49,691
[Haru] All right, here we go.

297
00:14:49,774 --> 00:14:50,609
[camera clicks]

298
00:14:52,068 --> 00:14:53,445
Thank you. You're so sweet.

299
00:14:53,528 --> 00:14:54,487
My pleasure.

300
00:14:54,571 --> 00:14:55,614
[Lisa chuckling excitedly]

301
00:14:55,697 --> 00:14:57,616
I can't believe you're actually friends
with him!

302
00:14:57,699 --> 00:14:58,950
- [chuckling nervously]
- Since when?

303
00:14:59,034 --> 00:15:00,577
All right, well, it's good to see you.

304
00:15:00,660 --> 00:15:01,745
What? You're leaving?

305
00:15:01,828 --> 00:15:04,080
Yeah, Lisa and I have shopping to do.

306
00:15:04,164 --> 00:15:06,374
- [Lisa] Aw. We can go another time!
- Huh?

307
00:15:06,458 --> 00:15:09,044
The mall's not going anywhere!
He's your friend, right?

308
00:15:09,127 --> 00:15:11,254
- Well, it's just--
- Stop it. Just stay and chat him up!

309
00:15:11,338 --> 00:15:13,465
Ah, he's busy! I thought we were shopping.

310
00:15:13,548 --> 00:15:16,509
Oh, we can do it another day.
See you back at school.

311
00:15:16,593 --> 00:15:18,261
- [Haru] Uh, okay...
- Later!

312
00:15:18,345 --> 00:15:20,764
[Haru] Well, I guess... Bye!

313
00:15:21,431 --> 00:15:24,351
It's kind of refreshing,
seeing you with a friend, Haru.

314
00:15:24,434 --> 00:15:27,771
[scoffs] That's not rude at all.
I've had friends since elementary school.

315
00:15:27,854 --> 00:15:29,898
I didn't mean to insult you.

316
00:15:31,066 --> 00:15:35,946
[Louis] <i>Wow... She might be just the person
I most wanted to see right now.</i>

317
00:15:36,029 --> 00:15:38,448
<i>From the very beginning, with Haru,</i>

318
00:15:38,531 --> 00:15:40,951
<i>I never had to be something I wasn't
with her.</i>

319
00:15:41,034 --> 00:15:43,036
Well, nice chatting with you.

320
00:15:43,119 --> 00:15:44,120
What?

321
00:15:44,204 --> 00:15:46,665
I... I need to get back. Assignments due.

322
00:15:46,748 --> 00:15:48,291
Let me walk with you.

323
00:15:53,463 --> 00:15:54,381
ODD SOUL FESTIVAL

324
00:15:54,464 --> 00:15:56,424
[Haru] Isn't this
pretty far out of the way for you?

325
00:15:56,508 --> 00:16:00,136
- [Louis] It's okay, it goes back around.
- Well, if you say so.

326
00:16:00,220 --> 00:16:02,305
You know,
Legoshi told me he takes this bus,

327
00:16:02,389 --> 00:16:04,349
even though his house
is nowhere near its route.

328
00:16:04,432 --> 00:16:05,266
[both laugh]

329
00:16:05,350 --> 00:16:06,184
[Louis] Stalker behavior.

330
00:16:06,267 --> 00:16:11,481
Legoshi is such a weirdo sometimes.
But I like it. [laughs]

331
00:16:11,564 --> 00:16:12,565
That's nice.

332
00:16:13,316 --> 00:16:15,193
[Louis] <i>It feels kind of strange.</i>

333
00:16:16,069 --> 00:16:19,864
<i>There was a time her white fur
and innocent face were so delicate</i>

334
00:16:19,948 --> 00:16:22,867
<i>I could've sworn she'd vanish
at any moment.</i>

335
00:16:22,951 --> 00:16:26,454
<i>But now, this rabbit is so defined.</i>

336
00:16:28,498 --> 00:16:31,918
Even though you and I didn't
end up together,

337
00:16:32,002 --> 00:16:34,045
I like the Haru you turned into.

338
00:16:34,129 --> 00:16:37,132
Uh... Really?

339
00:16:37,215 --> 00:16:38,717
Aren't I kind of a square?

340
00:16:38,800 --> 00:16:40,593
- What do you mean?
- Uh...

341
00:16:40,677 --> 00:16:44,556
Lately, I've been learning
to think before I leap.

342
00:16:44,639 --> 00:16:46,516
Before, no matter what I did,

343
00:16:46,599 --> 00:16:48,643
even if I got into trouble,
I'd just think,

344
00:16:48,727 --> 00:16:51,104
"stuff happens,"
and threw caution to the wind.

345
00:16:51,688 --> 00:16:56,067
But now I think...
"Is Legoshi worrying about me right now?"

346
00:16:56,151 --> 00:16:59,738
Ah. Well, yeah,
that's definitely not like the old Haru.

347
00:17:00,238 --> 00:17:04,117
{\an8}Changing for some guy
seems kind of corny if you ask me.

348
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:07,746
Doesn't being able to change like that
prove it's a good relationship?

349
00:17:07,829 --> 00:17:10,206
That's the corny stuff I'm talking about.

350
00:17:10,290 --> 00:17:13,168
[sighs]
But then I get caught up in the moment.

351
00:17:14,252 --> 00:17:15,086
[Melon groans]

352
00:17:15,170 --> 00:17:20,258
They were serving corn soup
for lunch today. It gets caught...

353
00:17:20,341 --> 00:17:22,177
[Haru exclaiming softly]

354
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:24,179
[Melon grunts softly]

355
00:17:26,723 --> 00:17:30,101
I had my doubts
you and I would cross paths again.

356
00:17:30,185 --> 00:17:33,313
Especially, of course, after being fired.

357
00:17:33,396 --> 00:17:35,190
This might be the last time
we see each other.

358
00:17:35,273 --> 00:17:38,026
Oh, uh, is that right? Sorry to hear that.

359
00:17:38,109 --> 00:17:39,903
[Melon laughs]

360
00:17:39,986 --> 00:17:42,697
If you're disappointed, I can't tell.

361
00:17:42,781 --> 00:17:45,200
Weird question for you, Professor...

362
00:17:45,283 --> 00:17:48,369
But are you mixed?
Carnivore and herbivore?

363
00:17:48,453 --> 00:17:52,123
[Melon] Hmm, how to respond to that...

364
00:17:52,207 --> 00:17:56,461
People who ask that
usually end up with a frown on their face.

365
00:17:56,544 --> 00:17:57,629
[chuckles excitedly]

366
00:17:57,712 --> 00:18:01,841
So then mixes can grow up
healthy and strong!

367
00:18:01,925 --> 00:18:03,760
Amazing! I'm so glad!

368
00:18:06,262 --> 00:18:08,848
{\an8}I was thrilled!
Because, you know, like,

369
00:18:08,932 --> 00:18:12,477
{\an8}if Legoshi and I wanted to have a child,
it sounds like it'd be okay, right?

370
00:18:12,560 --> 00:18:14,229
{\an8}Wait, uh, back up...

371
00:18:14,312 --> 00:18:16,314
Was he a mix of gazelle and leopard?

372
00:18:16,397 --> 00:18:19,776
[Haru] Yeah, you know, horns and all.
They go up and out like this.

373
00:18:19,859 --> 00:18:20,985
[Louis] Oh, that... uh--

374
00:18:21,069 --> 00:18:23,154
[Haru] Uh-huh. And he's got these...

375
00:18:23,238 --> 00:18:26,241
[Melon laughing]

376
00:18:26,324 --> 00:18:30,245
Somebody being happy I was born
is certainly a new one for me.

377
00:18:30,328 --> 00:18:32,872
I must say, you're really quite unusual.

378
00:18:32,956 --> 00:18:36,876
What? No way. It's normal.
We all celebrate birthdays.

379
00:18:36,960 --> 00:18:38,044
[Melon grunts softly]

380
00:18:38,128 --> 00:18:39,838
Well... [inhales]

381
00:18:39,921 --> 00:18:41,965
No one's ever celebrated mine before.

382
00:18:42,048 --> 00:18:42,924
No?

383
00:18:43,007 --> 00:18:45,176
It's on the same day as a festival.

384
00:18:45,260 --> 00:18:46,594
Oh, I see.

385
00:18:46,678 --> 00:18:50,723
What are you gonna do, right?
The Odd Soul Festival.

386
00:18:50,807 --> 00:18:56,563
A day to be thankful that herbivores
weren't eaten by carnivores. Eh.

387
00:18:56,646 --> 00:19:00,024
Ironic, that a mix like me
was born on that day.

388
00:19:00,108 --> 00:19:02,610
So your birthday's coming up soon then?

389
00:19:02,694 --> 00:19:05,989
Do you have a birthday wish?
You've gotta treat yourself!

390
00:19:06,072 --> 00:19:07,991
[Melon sighs demurely] Oh...

391
00:19:08,074 --> 00:19:10,243
You might be right.

392
00:19:11,035 --> 00:19:14,747
Hmm. What I really want is...

393
00:19:14,831 --> 00:19:16,875
[Haru] Yeah, yeah, I'm listening.

394
00:19:18,418 --> 00:19:19,252
What?

395
00:19:19,335 --> 00:19:22,422
He said that he wants to eat your flesh?

396
00:19:22,505 --> 00:19:23,965
STOPPING

397
00:19:24,591 --> 00:19:26,676
So, what did you say back then?

398
00:19:26,759 --> 00:19:27,635
I said, "Sure."

399
00:19:27,719 --> 00:19:29,888
- Huh?
- [chuckling nervously]

400
00:19:29,971 --> 00:19:31,806
I was caught off guard.

401
00:19:32,390 --> 00:19:35,143
Oh, uh... [chuckles nervously]

402
00:19:35,226 --> 00:19:37,270
A pinky promise?

403
00:19:39,063 --> 00:19:41,024
Uh... [chuckles nervously]

404
00:19:42,066 --> 00:19:43,860
Okay, you got it.

405
00:19:43,943 --> 00:19:45,570
[laughs]

406
00:19:45,653 --> 00:19:48,239
{\an8}Are you supposed to be some kind
of convenience store snack?

407
00:19:50,450 --> 00:19:52,202
[Haru] Oh, that's harsh.

408
00:19:52,285 --> 00:19:55,205
I'm more like a fancy desert
at a fine dining restaurant.

409
00:19:55,914 --> 00:19:59,375
Anyway, I'm fine being the kind of girl
who gives rather than takes.

410
00:19:59,459 --> 00:20:02,045
Herbivores are meant to be eaten, right?

411
00:20:02,128 --> 00:20:06,382
I never thought that one day I'd be
dealing with your prenuptial doubts.

412
00:20:07,634 --> 00:20:09,552
[Haru grunting]

413
00:20:10,094 --> 00:20:12,513
You're neither a snack, nor a dessert.

414
00:20:12,597 --> 00:20:15,308
You're neither herbivore,
nor are you prey.

415
00:20:15,391 --> 00:20:18,019
You are Haru. You're just yourself.

416
00:20:18,102 --> 00:20:21,856
Complain all you like.
Cry about it. Whatever.

417
00:20:21,940 --> 00:20:24,901
{\an8}But you have to keep living.
You have to live!

418
00:20:28,529 --> 00:20:30,490
I don't need you bossing me around.

419
00:20:30,573 --> 00:20:32,242
- Goodbye.
- [Louis exclaims]

420
00:20:32,325 --> 00:20:34,619
Wait! Haru!

421
00:20:35,620 --> 00:20:38,164
CENTRAL BUS SHIOKUMIZAKAUE

422
00:20:39,499 --> 00:20:42,543
There were tons of blueberries
growing behind the fountain,

423
00:20:42,627 --> 00:20:43,962
so I picked these.

424
00:20:44,045 --> 00:20:45,129
Uh-- Oh.

425
00:20:46,130 --> 00:20:47,340
[Pina sighs softly]

426
00:20:47,423 --> 00:20:50,969
Hey, Bill? What's going on? You okay?

427
00:20:51,928 --> 00:20:54,055
It was so full of life.

428
00:20:54,138 --> 00:20:56,933
Now it's just cold and still.

429
00:20:57,016 --> 00:20:58,518
[gentle music playing]

430
00:20:58,601 --> 00:21:00,103
[Bill] I'm sorry.

431
00:21:12,031 --> 00:21:14,117
There was a power outage.

432
00:21:14,200 --> 00:21:17,161
And because of that,
its heat lamp shut off.

433
00:21:18,079 --> 00:21:20,373
If it was going to die anyway,

434
00:21:20,456 --> 00:21:22,709
maybe you should've eaten it
right from the start.

435
00:21:22,792 --> 00:21:24,210
[Pina grunts]

436
00:21:24,294 --> 00:21:25,295
[groans softly]

437
00:21:25,962 --> 00:21:27,463
[grunts]

438
00:21:29,507 --> 00:21:30,717
Not funny.

439
00:21:38,558 --> 00:21:41,019
[Pina] <i>If you think about
eating and loving,</i>

440
00:21:41,102 --> 00:21:43,646
<i>both of them should bring us happiness.</i>

441
00:21:45,148 --> 00:21:49,610
<i>But when those two things intertwine,
someone always ends up getting hurt.</i>

442
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,999
[closing theme song playing]
